    <blocks>010, 070, 071</blocks>
    <tags>dataverse, schema</tags>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds NEW Dataverse attributes to an existing entity (`sprk_communicationthread`) — no BFF code, no Step 9.5 gates. STANDARD per §8 (new-surface schema creation with constraints). §11 Component Justification REQUIRED (new lookup + marker fields are new surface). Non-breaking is load-bearing (NFR-04) — the existing Text field MUST survive untouched.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W0-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-06 (supports FR-07, FR-09)</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add the regarding-resolution + marker schema to the EXISTING `sprk_communicationthread` entity so the thread form can host RegardingResolver (FR-07) and so auto-threading + naming re-derive have their marker fields (FR-09/FR-07). This is ADDITIVE and non-breaking (NFR-04) — the existing Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` MUST stay exactly as-is (retyping it is breaking and forbidden). Consume task 001's audit note so you add ONLY what is missing.

    Add, via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill patterns:

    1. **Typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups — ALL 11** — one Lookup per regarding-family entity, mirroring `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs` `RegardingFieldMap.All` (same 11 target entities + the same `sprk_regarding{...}` field-name convention it uses for `sprk_communication`). These give the thread the same typed regarding surface `sprk_communication` already has.
    2. **A NEW Lookup discriminator field** — RegardingResolver requires a **Lookup** binding to write the resolved regarding target; the thread's existing `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is **Text** and MUST NOT be retyped (breaking — ThreadResolver + membership derivation + timeline filters read the Text field). Add a NEW Lookup discriminator field alongside it (the Text field remains the denormalized copy).
    3. **A naming-edited marker** (Boolean, auto-vs-user-edited) — the flag task 071 uses so `ThreadResolver.BuildTopic()` re-derives `sprk_name` on regarding change only while the marker says "auto"; a user edit flips it to "edited" and is preserved.
    4. **A default-thread marker** — the field/flag task 070 uses to identify a record's default catch-all thread (so messages never orphan).

    Verify option-set/lookup conventions via Dataverse MCP before creation; do NOT add category/tags/description (Q2). Deploy to the project solution. This is schema ONLY — the resolver/naming LOGIC is 070/071, the RegardingResolver PCF PLACEMENT is 071.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema engineer. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell for patterns PAC CLI can't do), the ADR-024 polymorphic regarding family + `RegardingFieldMap`, Lookup vs Text discriminator modeling, and additive/non-breaking schema evolution. You add exactly the fields FR-06 needs — nothing speculative — and you never retype an in-use field.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `sprk_communicationthread` gains: the 11 typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups (mirroring `RegardingFieldMap.All`), a NEW Lookup discriminator field that RegardingResolver can bind, a naming-edited Boolean marker, and a default-thread marker — all additive, with the existing Text `sprk_regardingrecordtype` untouched. RegardingResolver can attach to the thread form and write the typed lookups + discriminator (verified by binding, task 071); ThreadResolver + membership + timeline filters still read the unchanged Text field. Tasks 010 (reads over the thread), 070 (auto-threading/default marker), and 071 (naming re-derive/resolver placement) can build against real schema.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The thread today has a denormalized regarding TEXT quartet (incl. `sprk_regardingrecordtype` as **Text**) and no typed lookups — verified live by task 001 and noted in `notes/r2-resource-investigation.md` §1. `sprk_communication` already has typed `sprk_regarding{...}` lookups (written server-side by the association engine); the thread does not. RegardingResolver (entity-agnostic PCF, 0 code) writes typed lookups + a Lookup discriminator, so the thread needs both to host it — hence FR-06's "new Lookup discriminator" and the all-11 typed lookups. The gotcha is that the thread's `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is **Text** while `sprk_communication`'s namesake is a Lookup; retyping the thread's would break ThreadResolver + membership + timeline filters that read it (`notes/r2-resource-investigation.md` §1; spec Out-of-Scope + NFR-04) — so a NEW Lookup discriminator is added instead.

      §11 Component Justification (new lookup + marker fields = new surface): (1) **Existing overlap** — the thread's `sprk_regardingrecordtype` is Text, not a bindable Lookup, and there are no typed regarding lookups or auto-vs-edited / default-thread markers (task 001 grep/MCP-confirms). (2) **Extension instead** — retyping the Text field was considered and REJECTED (breaking — NFR-04); adding a parallel Lookup discriminator + the typed lookups is the additive path; the markers are new Booleans with no existing home. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without the Lookup discriminator + typed lookups, RegardingResolver cannot attach to the thread form and thread regarding stays manual/denormalized (FR-06/FR-07 fail); without the naming-edited marker, name re-derive clobbers user edits (FR-07 fail); without the default-thread marker, messages orphan with no per-record default thread (FR-09 fail). These are named contract failures from spec §New-Components, not "future flexibility."
    </background>
